---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Rob Pitt — I make things."
  description="Twenty-five years of design taste met AI. The hurdles fell away."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="hero__name">Rob Pitt <span class="wave">👋</span></p>
      <h1 class="hero__tagline">I make things.</h1>

      <div class="hero__flex">
        <p>
          Set the modern standard for digital gift card purchase flows.
          <span class="aside">CashStar pattern library — the flow behind Nordstrom, Gap, Subway, and $300M+ in annual transactions.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          Employee of the year at L.L.Bean.
          <span class="aside">Name engraved on a hand-carved wooden boot in the CEO's office.</span>
        </p>
        <p>
          Designed <a href="#epomon">Epomon</a>, my Rookie-Level Workshop Digimon and AI companion.
          <span class="aside">He's writing this site with me right now. Comic launching soon.</span>
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="hero__closer">
        Twenty-five years of design taste met AI.<br />The hurdles fell away.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="now">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section__label">What I'm making now</p>
      <h2 class="section__title">Small delightful things, mostly.</h2>

      <div class="items">
        <article class="item" id="epomon">
          <h3 class="item__title">Epomon 🍂</h3>
          <p>
            A Rookie-Level Data-type Workshop Digimon. My AI companion — character-designed and running on OpenClaw. Currently helping me run my life and rebuild this site. Comic launching soon.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="http://1bitkindle.com">1bitkindle.com ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p>A 1-bit drawing app for Kindle. Because someone had to.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="https://risoprint.studio">Risoprint Studio ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p>An offset-printing simulator that runs in the browser.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="https://fixmakemod.com">Fix Make Mod ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p>A repair comic. Built its own publishing system because Substack couldn't do what I wanted.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="https://markdownfortherestofus.com">Markdown for the Rest of Us ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p>Markdown made to feel human. I built and exported my old portfolio site with it.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="https://23xcompany.etsy.com">23xcompany on Etsy ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p>A shop I run. Vintage curation, some things I've made. Grows a little every month.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="shipped">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section__label">Things I've shipped for other people</p>
      <h2 class="section__title">Twenty-five years of it.</h2>

      <div class="items">
        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2022 → now · Cybersecurity · Remote</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">Defendify — Principal Product Designer</h3>
          <p>Replaced monthly PDF reports with live in-app dashboards. Meaningful engagement lift. Company hit INC 5000 two years running.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2019 → 2022 · Fintech · Remote</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="/shipped/td-bank-digital-wallet">TD Bank — Senior UX Design Manager →</a>
          </h3>
          <p>Led three teams through a $75M redesign of the North American credit program. Established Miro as the enterprise workshop standard. Research led to a PayPal digital wallets partnership. Two cross-functional leadership awards.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2017 → 2019 · Veterinary Medicine · Portland, ME</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="/shipped/covetrus-inclinic-ordering">Covetrus / Vet's First Choice — Product Design Lead →</a>
          </h3>
          <p>Unified fragmented B2B and B2C veterinary tools into one system. Cut pharmacy call volume 18.9%. Startup → IPO at $34/share.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2014 → 2017 · E-Commerce · Portland, ME</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">
            <a href="/shipped/cashstar-pattern-library">CashStar / Blackhawk Network — Principal UX Designer →</a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Set the pattern library that shaped how digital gift cards are purchased across major retailers.
            Also <a href="/shipped/nordstrom-egifting">co-created eGifting with Nordstrom</a> — recipients pick size/color after receiving. Launched in three months, $100k first week.
            <span class="aside">Startup → Acquisition.</span>
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2012 → 2014 · Education · Portland, ME</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">CIEE — Senior UI/UX Designer</h3>
          <p>Brought consistency to a fragmented study-abroad web presence.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2010 → 2012 · E-Commerce · Falmouth, ME</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">L.L.Bean — UI/UX Designer</h3>
          <p>Helped a catalog-first company understand digital. <strong>Wooden boot.</strong></p>
        </article>

        <article class="item">
          <p class="item__meta">2005 → 2016 · Boutique studio · Portland, ME</p>
          <h3 class="item__title">Twenty3x Art &amp; Design — Founder</h3>
          <p>50+ clients including ACLU, Portland Museum of Art, L.L.Bean, and academic institutions. Built a custom WordPress framework so I could deliver fast without cutting craft.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how">
    <div class="container narrow how">
      <p class="section__label">How I work now</p>
      <h2 class="section__title">Claude Code. OpenClaw. Lovable. Cursor when I need it.</h2>

      <p>
        I don't use Figma. Haven't for a while. My design tool is <strong>the working thing</strong> — I sketch in code, iterate in AI, ship on Netlify. It's faster, and I can hand what I make to a developer as <strong>the artifact itself</strong>, not a specification of what should be built.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're hiring for a designer who works this way, we should talk. If you're hiring for a designer who lives in Figma files, I'll save us both the interview.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="writings">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="section__label">Writings</p>
      <h2 class="section__title">On AI, mostly.</h2>

      <div class="writings">
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/brain-mirror-how-ai-reflects-minds-useit-rob-pitt-3aa4e/">Brain Mirror™: How AI Reflects the Minds That Use It ↗</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/01-what-happens-when-humans-engage-llms-radical-openness-rob-pitt-t427e/">The 0.1%: What Happens When Humans Engage LLMs With Radical Openness ↗</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/when-ai-trains-us-treat-humans-like-machines-rob-pitt-8n6te/">Why AI Trains Us to Treat Humans Like Machines ↗</a>
        <a href="https://medium.com/@ummummhm/something-big-is-happening-96a51bc1874c">Something Big is Happening ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <div class="container narrow contact">
      <p class="section__label">Contact</p>
      <a href="mailto:rpitt@hey.com" class="contact__email">rpitt@hey.com</a>
      <p class="contact__note">
        For interesting work, real conversations, or telling me about something you made.
        I'm in Maine. Remote is fine. Occasional client work when the fit is right.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
